HST Office: form macros run after reopening .ods and .odt.

Calc stored the VBA mode in the document settings but not the project name, as Writer does. After
reopening, the name was empty, UserForm1.Show asked for the dialog ".UserForm1" and failed with a
Basic error, and VBA export could not find the project. The name is now stored as VBAProjectName;
files saved before use a library named VBAProject.

A library loaded on demand had a second problem, seen in .odt: loading replaces placeholder elements,
and BasMgrContainerListenerImpl::elementReplaced() made the missing module without its module info.
A form module became a plain module, and UserForm1.Caption failed with "property or method not found".

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba-form-events.py.
---
--- a/basic/source/basmgr/basmgr.cxx
+++ b/basic/source/basmgr/basmgr.cxx
@@ -262,7 +262,17 @@
     if( pMod )
             pMod->SetSource( aMod );
     else
+    {
+        // HST: loading a library replaces its placeholder elements, and a form module made without
+        // its module info is a plain module, so UserForm1 had no form. Only forms change here:
+        // other module types of a library loaded this way stay as they were.
+        uno::Reference< vba::XVBAModuleInfo > xVBAModuleInfo( Event.Source, uno::UNO_QUERY );
+        if ( xVBAModuleInfo.is() && xVBAModuleInfo->hasModuleInfo( aName )
+             && xVBAModuleInfo->getModuleInfo( aName ).ModuleType == ModuleType::FORM )
+            pLib->MakeModule( aName, xVBAModuleInfo->getModuleInfo( aName ), aMod );
+        else
             pLib->MakeModule( aName, aMod );
+    }
 
     pLib->SetModified( false );
 }
